1
00:00:00,986 --> 00:00:06,576
VibeGuard: a harness that learns its own guardrails. Only a human can loosen them.

2
00:00:09,144 --> 00:00:14,284
Memory seeded into Atlas: failure taxonomy and lexicon, embedded for vector search.

3
00:00:14,484 --> 00:00:19,834
Run one, no rules: most tasks fail. Each failure proposes a rule.

4
00:00:20,034 --> 00:00:25,314
A human approves. Every transition writes a receipt; nothing is deleted.

5
00:00:25,514 --> 00:00:29,254
Held-out tasks are only measured, never used to write rules.

6
00:00:29,454 --> 00:00:36,394
Three rules live: runaway paid calls, hardcoded secrets, destructive commands. Zero false blocks.

7
00:00:36,594 --> 00:00:40,654
Held-out pass rate: one of six to six of six over five runs.

8
00:00:40,854 --> 00:00:44,834
Provenance: the failing attempt and the detector, attached to the rule.

9
00:00:45,034 --> 00:00:48,414
Every run is episodic memory with per-task traces.

10
00:00:48,614 --> 00:00:56,964
COSTAR scores the prompt and emits a form: which questions to ask before money is spent. Vector search maps take payments to payment integration.

11
00:00:57,164 --> 00:01:05,494
Four memory types in Atlas, mirrored into Agent Engine memory, deployed on Modelence. Agents tighten their own leash; only humans loosen it.

